## Recommended code additions

### A. Add a new API to worker state
The worker should expose:
- `last_status`
- `last_failure_category`
- `last_error_message`
- `position_reliability`
- `state`

This lets the GUI show exact state and user-safe messaging.

### B. Add a `safe_to_move` helper
```python
def safe_to_move(self) -> bool:
    return self.state not in {CameraState.UNSYNCED, CameraState.ERROR, CameraState.PAUSED} and self.position_reliability != PositionReliability.UNSYNCED
```

### C. Add state transitions for manual override and recovery
- `PAUSED` blocks auto-schedules
- `UNSYNCED` blocks automatic movement
- `RECOVERING` should try `Stop()`, then `Home()`, then read status if supported

